      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Does our data ever leave our environment?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "No. Deepvine is deployed inside your firm's own infrastructure, and your client records, accounts, and prompts stay there. The system connects to your existing tools and reads your data in place; nothing is copied to a shared cloud, and your inputs are never used to train models that other organizations touch."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can we use it with our CRM and portfolio systems?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes. Deepvine is built to connect to the systems an RIA already runs on, including your CRM, portfolio and planning tools, email, and Slack. Rather than asking advisers to upload files into a separate tool, it indexes the firm's existing repositories so answers are grounded in the actual client record."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What happens to the system if we end the engagement?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "You keep your data and the knowledge base built on it, because both live in your environment from day one. Deepvine runs on infrastructure you control, so ending the engagement means we stop managing and maintaining the system, not that your firm's institutional memory walks out the door with a vendor."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How long does backfill take?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Backfill timing depends on the volume and format of your historical client records, but the connection and initial indexing are typically measured in weeks, not months. Once the backfill completes, daily diffs keep the system current as new documents and messages are created."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Does this satisfy our compliance obligations?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Deepvine is designed to support your obligations under Rule 204-2 and amended Regulation S-P, but no vendor can guarantee compliance on your firm's behalf. A private deployment removes the hardest parts of the analysis by keeping client information in your control and out of shared model training; your firm remains responsible for its own recordkeeping, oversight, and security decisions."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What does it cost?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Pricing depends on firm size, the systems being connected, and the depth of historical backfill, so we scope it during the demo rather than list a single number. The engagement is structured as an ongoing managed service that includes deployment, maintenance, and updates."
      }
    }
  ]
}

